{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "list_id": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "run": 3,
  "simulation_id": "sim-02",
  "member_id": "mehlig-bernhard",
  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B014",
        "laureates": [
          "Alexander A. Belavin",
          "Alexander B. Zamolodchikov",
          "Alexander M. Polyakov"
        ],
        "citation": "for foundational advances in two-dimensional conformal field theory and exact critical phenomena"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B007",
    "B043"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. B014 identifies an unusually clean instance in which symmetry exposes exact and universal structure in systems otherwise governed by complex collective fluctuations. Two-dimensional conformal field theory made critical phenomena quantitatively intelligible while establishing a durable connection between statistical physics and quantum field theory. The proposed three theorists form a coherent attribution to the foundational advance.",
    "case_against": "The theory is abstract, and its subsequent development involved a broad community. We must therefore ensure that the citation stays with the foundational two-dimensional framework and that the three names faithfully represent the relevant priority boundary.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "eriksson-olle",
        "point": "Eriksson argues that B007 is a mature framework with extensive connection to spectra and properties of correlated materials, while accepting that it is controlled only in particular limits.",
        "response": "I continue to regard B007 as an excellent alternative, especially for its constructive dialogue with experiment. Its limited controlled domain is nevertheless not merely a wording issue: it means the achievement is a powerful self-consistent approximation outside that domain. B014 instead establishes exact universal results, which is the more fundamental and sharply bounded physical contribution."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "johansson-goran",
        "point": "Johansson emphasizes that B043 rests on a clean magic-wavelength idea, demonstrated performance, and independent reproducibility across laboratories.",
        "response": "These are compelling virtues, and B043 has strengthened as the clearest experimental alternative in the discussion. Yet its final framing still depends on separating the lattice-clock innovation from the longer atomic-clock lineage and resolving whether two names are complete. I place the exact conceptual reorganization achieved by B014 ahead of this otherwise exceptionally mature measurement advance."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "lindroth-eva",
        "point": "Lindroth argues that B023 should be framed around repeatedly demonstrated trapped-ion control and simulation, rather than unachieved scalable fault-tolerant computation.",
        "response": "That narrower framing substantially improves B023 and recognizes a genuine experimental achievement. Even so, the division of foundational credit across protocols, platforms, and experimental lineages remains difficult to compress into three names. B014 retains a more unified discovery and attribution within the available configuration."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether archival review confirms that Belavin, Zamolodchikov, and Polyakov alone provide the appropriate compact attribution for the foundational two-dimensional conformal-field-theory advance.",
      "Whether the committee should give priority this year to exact theoretical understanding over the experimentally mature precision-measurement case represented by B043."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "Unchanged: I share the Gothenburg physics environment with committee colleagues Göran Johansson and Eva Olsson; the supplied profile identifies no specific collaboration."
  }
}
